The GEOS DAS has used two different methods of calculating aircraft bias correction coefficients
One method runs 'cft_update.f' after the analysis step to update bias coefficients offline.
This method only calculates a single value based on a weighted mean of the temperature difference
between the aircraft observations with a given tail ID and the forecast background value at a
particular location.  This method was used in the MERRA-2 reanalysis.
The second method uses the variational aircraft bias coefficient calculation developed at NCEP,
and calculates three coefficients - a mean coefficient (constant predictor = 1), and two
additional coefficients for the ascent rate and ascent rate squared predictors (Zhu, et al, 2015).

The format of the original bias coefficient file as used in MERRA2 is
1 - tail ID
2 - aircraft bias correction (K) used by analysis
3 - error estimate for bias coefficient
4 - running count of obs used for bias calculation
5 - calculated bias correction (K)
6 - mean departure of temperature obs from background (K)
7 - standard deviation of departure from background (K)
8 - number of observations used to calculate (6)
Optional fields
9 - number of consecutive synoptic times tail number has appeared
10 - count of synoptic times missing for tail number

When the variational bias correction code was added to the GSI the format of the
offline bias coefficient file was changed to be comaptible with the new bias format.
1 - tail ID
2 - index for tail ID
3 - aircraft bias correction (K) used by analysis
4 - zero  (unused second predictor coefficient)
5 - zero  (unused third  predictor coefficient)
6 - running count of obs used for bias calculation
7 - zero  (unused count for second predictor)
8 - zero  (unused count for third predictor)
9 - error estimate for bias coefficient
10 - zero  (unused slot for second predictor)
11 - zero  (unused slot for third  predictor)
12 - YYYYMM time indicator
13 - actual bias value calculated
14 - mean departure of temperature obs from background (K)
15 - standard deviation of departure from background (K)
16 - number of observations used to calculate (14)
Optional fields
17 - number of consecutive synoptic times tail number has appeared
18 - count of synoptic times missing for tail number

Format of NCEP method bias coefficient file
1 - tail ID
2 - index for tail ID
3 - coefficient for mean predictor
4 - coefficient for ascent rate predictor
5 - coefficient for ascent rate squared predictor
6 - number of observations used in predictor estimate
7 - zero  (unused count for second predictor)
8 - zero  (unused count for third predictor)
9 - background error for mean coefficient
10 - background error for ascent rate coefficient
11 - background error for ascent rate squared coefficient
12 - YYYYMM time indicator


